VERDICT: if corr(L, facet-deficit) is NEGATIVE or near 0, the facet-breaks do NOT predict
L (bigger structural break can mean SMALLER L). Then NO joint of the facets lower-bounds L
=> the joint rigidity FAILS: the facets measure structural distance-from-AP, L measures
safe-set openness, and they DISAGREE. The residue is irreducibly metric, not even jointly
reducible to the structural facets. Honest end of the 'joint rigidity' idea.
